#: src/algebra/definitions.md:123
msgid "Debit and credit decomposition"
msgstr "借方と貸方への分解"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:125
msgid "**Definition 8.** An exchange algebra extends the redundant algebra with side decompositions. Debit decomposition selects debit postings (left), and credit decomposition selects credit postings (right). For example, a decrease in cash is a credit, and an increase in an ordinary expense is a debit. An element is balanced when its exact debit and credit totals agree."
msgstr "**定義 8.** 交換代数は, 冗長代数に貸借分解を加えたものです. 借方分解は借方の項 (左側) を選び, 貸方分解は貸方の項 (右側) を選びます. 例えば, 現金の減少は貸方であり, 通常の費用の増加は借方です. 借方と貸方の厳密な合計が一致するとき, 要素は貸借が一致しています."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:127
msgid "Usage: [Recover the debit and credit columns](../overview.md#recover-the-debit-and-credit-columns)."
msgstr "使い方: [借方列と貸方列を取り出す](../overview.md#recover-the-debit-and-credit-columns)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:129
msgid "For transfers and journals, see Appendix A of [_Accounting State Space as a Foundation for Economic Agent-Based Modeling: An Input–Output Benchmark and Inventory Extension_](https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-8485050/v2)."
msgstr "振替と仕訳帳については, [_Accounting State Space as a Foundation for Economic Agent-Based Modeling: An Input–Output Benchmark and Inventory Extension_](https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-8485050/v2) の Appendix A を参照してください."

